**proposition 14.10 (ROC scope).** The identities THS1-THS6 and ROC1-ROC9 leave the actual set of primes with h_p>=2 undetermined. In particular, a vanishing theorem for D_(p,1) on a specified prime family would exclude WSS in that family, while an independently constructed member would give a WSS prime; neither existence nor vanishing on a new family follows from the displayed counts alone.

